+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+On the project's adversarial synthetic corpus built from a 30-word frequent
+vocabulary, the full-recall path had a measured p95 of **35.53 ms** before the
+term-selection fix. It queried BM25 with the first 24 prompt terms.
+
+The fix was to rank usable prompt terms by inverse document frequency (IDF) and
+query BM25 with only the eight highest-IDF terms, dropping terms absent from the
+store and very high-frequency terms that carry little signal. With that fix,
+the measured full-recall p95 was **8.75 ms**.
+
+These are the paired before/after p95 measurements recorded in the project's
+own stage breakdown (`[H6]` in `research/00-evidence-log.md`). The separately
+recorded 4.31 ms p95 (`[I3]`) is an end-to-end Rust hook measurement on a
+50,000-record index and is not the paired adversarial-corpus result above.
